              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Janet Shum"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Crispy, yummy, quick, and delicious! I can't stop eating them, so yes these are really good! I love them!",
            "datePublished": "2012-11-12T06:13:09.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sarika"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a 5 star recipe as is, but I added a pinch of nut meg and a little bit cinnamon for more flavor. They didn't spread much I used real butter at room temperature. The bake time was close to 12 min.",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-03T10:23:42.303Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "checkitout"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made these yesterday. They did expand quite a bit (not in a bad way) and the batch made 32. I took them out of the oven while they were still a bit soft but my son still thought they were too crunchy for his liking. Not hard but crunchy. The flavor was good and they came out perfectly round. Very easy to make.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-09T10:26:52.857Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CookieCritter"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are delicious! I made the recipe as is, no alterations. They did not spread too much at all. I wouldn't call them \"snaps\" because they are chewy, but I prefer chewy cookies so they're perfect. Unlike other reviewers, I didn't have a problem with the cookies spreading too much. I used real butter and softened it by smashing it up with a wooden spoon rather than the microwave. That might be why they didn't get super thin in the oven.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-02T20:19:40.330Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LEXI, JACK and COOKIE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good! Initially, I thought that dropping the dough by 1/2 teaspoon increments wasn't large enough, but it definitely is, so don't make my mistake and drop by 1 teaspoon increments; this dough spreads quite a bit. I'm going to add some coconut the next time I make these. As written though, this is a fabulous recipe! Thanks for sharing it.",
            "datePublished": "2010-06-09T09:01:42.437Z"
